    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'm also worried about my heart rate being picked up through the cushion. if they're using something like ballistocardiography or sensing vibrations, is there any way to mask that? like, would using a seat cushion with a specific density or wearing certain types of clothes change the way my pulse is transmitted to the sensors?",
